The set references Models/A330-303-GE.xml, which references
Models/A330-303-main.xml. Its aircraft geometry is a330-300-main.ac; the
included a333-animations.xml defines exterior animation, and cf6-80e1.xml and
cf6-80e1.ac define both GE engines. The PNGs are the individual AC texture
references. Other referenced FlightGear models, effects, scripts and cockpit
are NOT included; this is not a complete FlightGear aircraft distribution.

These files are passenger exterior assets. Passenger windows are painted into
323_blank.png and 303_blank.png; the latter also contains the GE nacelle UVs.
They cannot be turned into windowless cargo aircraft merely by hiding meshes.
The locally generated derived/323_windowless.png is an experimental modification
of 323_blank.png, distributed under the same GPL-2.0 terms. The accompanying
generate_windowless.py and window-footprints.json document how only 128 dark
and 10 outlined passenger windows were removed. All pixels outside the window
footprints and one-pixel halos are unmodified; no upstream originals were
changed. The GE engine UVs remain in the original 303_blank.png. This is a
windowless A330-300 passenger skin, not a factory A330-200F or an accurate
certified freighter conversion. An earlier, local software-rendered comparison predates the 14 liveries and
the approximate cargo door; that research image is not part of this release.

